+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional ``canonical`` option gives the type
+   represented by the alias and is displayed in the signature after ``=``.
+   Its expression is parsed as a type annotation, so referenced types are
+   cross-referenced. A description may be given in the directive body. The
+   directive also works inside a class description, where the class is part of
+   the alias's qualified name.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical: type expression
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the type represented by the alias. This option is optional.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined. The default value is
+      the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
